1(c) DASHBOARD - NOT MET.  Two distinct defects.

  (i) No test asserts the dashboard's funding projection at all.
      TestAccountsCard_SuppressedDuplicateCountedOnce
      (accounts_card_test.go:412-521) asserts only "$619.57", absence of
      "960.86", and absence of "low-balance threshold". Its fixture has two
      rows total, so accounts.Project receives an empty recurring slice and
      the projection line is exercised only vacuously. Nothing in the
      dashboard package asserts Crossing / SuggestedTopUp / Minimum under a
      resolved duplicate.

  (ii) The projection IS still contaminated by the suppressed row, via the
      recurring input. dashboard/handlers.go:114 filters the balance
      argument but passes the RAW `data` to detectRecurringForDashboard,
      which calls insights.DetectRecurringAt on the unfiltered set
      (internal/handlers/dashboard/accounts_card.go:241). The MCP twin
      recurringForProjection (internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/accounts.go:283)
      does apply .Active().

      Demonstrated, not reasoned. Probe fixture (scratch copy, R3 fix intact):
        account "checking", anchor 2026-05-01 = $4000, threshold $500
        checking-a.csv: 2026-06-01 Lucid -900.00 Scheduled Bill Pay
                        2026-07-01 Lucid -900.00 Scheduled Bill Pay
                        2026-08-01 Lucid -950.00 Scheduled Bill Pay
        checking-b.csv: 2026-08-02 Check #55501 -950.00 Posted
        Resolved via dl.SaveDuplicateDecision(kept=check, suppressed=Aug-1
        Lucid, kept_winner) - the same real workflow the worker's own tests
        use. asOf = MaxDate = 2026-08-02.

      Probe output (go test -run TestZZProbe_RecurringContamination -v
      ./internal/handlers/dashboard/):
        PROBE rows=4 suppressed=1 active=3
        PROBE RAW recurring (dashboard input): 1 item(s)
           desc="lucid" amount=916.67 freq=monthly occ=3 last=2026-08-01
           next=2026-09-01
        PROBE ACTIVE recurring (mcp input): 0 item(s)
        PROBE projection dashboard(raw recurring):
           available=true min=333.33 crossing=2026-09-01 topup=200.00
        PROBE projection mcp-equivalent(active recurring):
           available=true min=1250.00 crossing=(none) topup=0.00
        PROBE rendered card: Accounts USAA Checking Data through Aug 2, 2026
           $1,250.00 Drops below $500 around Sep 1, 2026 - no prior transfers
           to reference. Suggested top-up: $200.

      The suppressed $950 row is the third leg that turns a two-payment
      history into a "monthly" series, and its amount is averaged into
      Amount=916.67. Remove it (the .Active() counterfactual) and there is
      no recurring item and no crossing at all. The dashboard therefore
      renders a low-balance crossing and a $200 top-up recommendation that
      exist solely because of the row the user already resolved as a
      duplicate.

      The MCP path on the IDENTICAL fixture is clean, through the real tool:
        go test -run TestZZProbe_MCPRecurringContamination -v
                ./internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/
        PROBE MCP projection: available=true min=1250.00 crossing="" topup=0.00
        PROBE MCP get_accounts: balance=1250.00 low=false

      So the two paths disagree on the same data, and the dashboard is the
      wrong one. Criterion 1(c) is not met on the dashboard path.

